// BT-3367 fixture: a sealed Value class with a class-side factory method that
// is not itself declared `class sealed` — the shape that triggered the
// REPL-only dispatch bug (a class-level `sealed` flag leaking into every
// class method's own is_sealed bit when the class is recovered from
// already-loaded BEAM metadata, wrongly enabling the BT-1639 direct-call
// optimization for a method that constructs `self`).
sealed Value subclass: Bt3367SealedResult
  field: checkName = ""
  field: details = ""

  class ok: aName details: aDetails =>
    Bt3367SealedResult checkName: aName details: aDetails
